Ladybird’s generated background page puts the background scripts in its
body, after a head that holds only the charset. All three engines do the
same. Chromium’s GenerateBackgroundPageContents() and WebKit’s
WebExtension::generatedBackgroundContent() both emit a doctype and an
open body tag, then the scripts, and Gecko’s WebExtensionPolicy::
BackgroundPageHTML() emits a head with the charset meta, then a body
holding the scripts, so the body exists while any of them runs.
